    "result_text": "The full suite (a single acceptance test class) passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the existing Spring PetClinic conventions:\n\n**1. API contract \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from this at build time)\n- Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n- Added a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema.\n\n**2. Domain model \u2014 `Owner.java`**\n- Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n- Added a `@Transient getSalutation()` deriving `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is present. This lives alongside the other derived owner getters (`getInitials`, `getMembershipNumber`, etc.), keeping the single-responsibility structure intact.\n\n**3. Wiring** \u2014 no mapper changes needed: MapStruct auto-maps `title \u2192 title` (input) and `getSalutation() \u2192 salutation` (output) by name, reusing the existing mapping mechanism rather than adding an expression.\n\n**4. Schema** \u2014 added the `title` column to all four DDL scripts (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) since `ddl-auto=none` relies on `schema.sql`.\n\nDesign notes:\n- Placed `title` on `Owner` rather than the shared `Person` superclass, since `Vet` also extends `Person` and adding the column there would require touching the `vets` table/queries for no benefit \u2014 the salutation is an owner-facing concern here.\n- Kept `title` a plain string (with an example listing MR/MRS/MS/DR in the API description) rather than a generated enum, so the salutation reflects exactly the supplied value with no enum\u2194String conversion.",
